course: dictionary
lesson: 13930
title: Who makes the laws?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A legislature is a group of elected people who make the laws of a country or state. The word comes from the Latin for law, so it points straight to laws.
explain: «The legislature voted on the new law about school buses.» The clue is «voted» and «law»: the people who vote on new laws are the legislature. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The group of elected people voted on the new law" still makes sense, so the meaning fits.
explain: Every country has its own legislature. The UK has Parliament, the USA has Congress, and Ireland has the Oireachtas. Canada's provinces each have their own legislature too. The names are different, but the job is the same: making laws.
fact: A legislature is the group of elected people who make the laws.
fact: «Legislature» comes from a Latin word meaning law.
fact: The UK Parliament, the US Congress and the Irish Oireachtas are all legislatures.
fact: Canadian provinces each have their own legislature to make laws for their own province.
fact: The people in a legislature are elected, which means voters choose them.
exercise: «The legislature voted to pass the new law.» What is a legislature? | A book of old school rules | A court where judges decide crimes | *A group of elected people who make the laws | A group of police officers who catch thieves
exercise: Which of these is a legislature in the UK? | A bank | The police | The High Court | *Parliament
exercise: Ellie says, «The Congress in the USA is a legislature.» Why is she right? | Because it has a lot of desks | Because it is a big building in Washington | *Because elected people there make the laws | Because it is a court where people are tried
test: «The state legislature will meet in the capital next month.» What does legislature mean here? | A type of road | A school for young lawyers | A group of farmers who grow food | *A group of elected people who make laws
test: Which word is closest in meaning to legislature? | Playground | *Parliament | Library | Cathedral
exam: Why does a legislature matter to citizens? | It decides what is for dinner in school | It is the name of a type of voting card | It is a building where people go to watch films | *It is the group of elected people who make the laws we all must follow
